.DS_Store
.idea
*.log
tmp/

*.tern-port
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm
.eslintcache

.gemi
.env
.debug

# The artifacts of `prisma/postgres-only.prisma`, which only exist during a
# Postgres run — see `app/models/postgres.sh`. Uncommitted on purpose, unlike
# `app/models/generated/`: they carry a whole generated Prisma client, and the
# models they describe cannot be generated at all on SQLite, so a committed copy
# would be a directory that half the CI matrix could neither produce nor check.
app/models/generated-lists/

# The Prisma client gemi's differential harness compares against, generated from
# `prisma/differential.prisma`. Uncommitted for the same reason as above — it is
# a whole generated client — and produced by:
#
#     bunx prisma generate --schema prisma/differential.prisma
#
# An application never has one of these: `prisma/schema.prisma` has no
# `generator client` block, which is what lets an app install `prisma` alone.
app/models/prisma-client/

# The root `dev.db` only, and deliberately not `prisma/dev.db`.
#
# `prisma/dev.db` is a COMMITTED FIXTURE: `app/models/User.test.ts` copies it to
# a temp file and runs the whole ORM pipeline against the template's real schema.
# Ignoring it breaks fifteen tests on a clean checkout.
#
# The root copy is the artifact of a bug rather than anything's output. Before
# 0.65, gemi resolved a relative `file:` url against the process cwd while Prisma
# resolved it against the schema directory, so the dev server created an empty
# `dev.db` here and queried it. Nothing writes it now, and the entry stays so an
# upgrading checkout does not suddenly show one.
dev.db
dev.db-journal
dev.db-wal
dev.db-shm
